.TH STORMBYTE-STAGEMANAGER 1 "September 2026" "StormByte 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
StormByte-StageManager \- manage Gentoo stage tarballs, chroots, caches and downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B StormByte-StageManager
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B StormByte-StageManager
manages Gentoo stage3 (and similar) environments stored as compressed tarballs.
It can list stages, enter a chroot, rebase into a new filename, stream-recompress
or export stages, delete or rename them, download official stage3 images, and
attach free-form notes.
.PP
.B use
and
.B rebase
need root (mounts and
.BR chroot ).
If the invoking user is not root, the script re-execs itself with
.B sudo \-E
so
.BR DRY_RUN ,
.BR FORCE ,
.B SKIP_CACHE
and
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
survive.
After writes, new stage files and FILE-cache sidecars packed by this process
are
.BR chown ed
to
.B SUDO_UID:SUDO_GID
when those variables are set.
The process does
.B not
drop root inside the chroot.
.PP
.BR list ,
.BR convert ,
.BR export ,
.BR delete ,
.BR rename ,
.BR download ,
.B notes
and
.B config
do not require root if the invoking user can read and write
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER
(and the export destination).
.PP
Temporary work for
.B use
/
.B rebase
is performed under a configurable storage backend
.RB ( folder ,
.BR tmpfs ,
or
.BR zram ).
.B convert
and
.B export
ignore
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM
and
.B STORAGE_SIZE :
they never extract the tree and never mount tmpfs/zram.
.PP
Optional bind mounts expose host package caches, distfiles, repositories,
Portage patches and extra paths inside the chroot.
.PP
Optional
.B ccache
and
.B sccache
support can use either a host bind mount or a packed sidecar
.RI ( ccache.tbz2
/
.IR sccache.tbz2 )
under
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
In
.B FILE
mode the sidecar is expanded into a
.B shared tmpfs
workspace so several concurrent
.B use
/
.B rebase
sessions can share the same hot cache; the
.B last
session to exit packs the workspace back into the sidecar
.B even if
the user declines saving stage changes.
.PP
Inside the chroot, cache environment is injected transparently
.RB ( CCACHE_DIR ,
.BR FEATURES+=ccache ,
.BR SCCACHE_DIR ,
and related variables) without writing those settings into the stage tree.
.PP
Configuration is loaded by
.B loadConfig
from
.IR functions.sh :
.I ${workdir}/${self}.conf
first, then
.IR /etc/conf.d/${self}.conf .
Requires
.B StormByte-functions-bash
≥ 1.3.0.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/StormByte-StageManager.conf
System-wide configuration. A copy next to the executable is accepted
(same search order
.B loadConfig
uses).
.PP
Main variables (keys and meaning unchanged from 1.x):
.TP
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
Absolute path where stage tarballs are stored.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM
.BR folder ,
.BR tmpfs ,
.BR zram ,
or
.B auto
(try zram, then tmpfs, then folder). Used by
.B use
/
.B rebase
only.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SIZE
Size for
.B tmpfs
/
.B zram
(e.g.
.BR 20G ,
.BR 512M ).
Also the default size for shared FILE cache tmpfs workspaces when
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
/
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
are unset.
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM_ZRAM_COMPRESSION_ALGO
Optional zram algorithm:
.BR zstd ,
.BR lz4 ,
or
.BR lz4hc .
Empty keeps the kernel default.
.TP
.B TARBALL_NOTE_EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "notes edit" .
.TP
.B DETACH_NOTE_EDITOR
.B YES
to background the editor,
.B NO
otherwise.
.TP
.B GZIP_COMPRESSION_LEVEL\fR / \fBBZIP_COMPRESSION_LEVEL\fR / \fBXZ_COMPRESSION_LEVEL
Integer
.B 1
to
.BR 9 .
.TP
.B ZSTD_COMPRESSION_LEVEL
Integer
.B 1
to
.BR 19 .
.SS Compiler caches (ccache / sccache)
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE
.B YES
or
.BR NO .
If
.BR YES ,
exactly one of
.B USE_CCACHE_BIND
or
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE
must be
.BR YES .
.TP
.B CCACHE_DIR
Path used as the cache directory inside the stage (and as the host path when
.BR USE_CCACHE_BIND=YES ).
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE_BIND
Bind-mount the host
.B CCACHE_DIR
into the stage.
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE
Use the packed sidecar
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/ccache.tbz2
via a shared tmpfs workspace.
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE
.B YES
or
.BR NO .
If
.BR YES ,
exactly one of
.B USE_SCCACHE_BIND
or
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE
must be
.BR YES .
.TP
.B SCCACHE_DIR
Path used as the sccache directory inside the stage (and as the host path when
.BR USE_SCCACHE_BIND=YES ).
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE_BIND
Bind-mount the host
.B SCCACHE_DIR
into the stage.
.TP
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE
Use the packed sidecar
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/sccache.tbz2
via a shared tmpfs workspace.
.TP
.B SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE
Maximum sccache disk budget passed into the chroot (default
.BR 20G ).
.SS Other paths and binds
.TP
.B PKG_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_PKG_BIND
Binary package directory and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B DISTFILES_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_DISTFILES_BIND
Distfiles directory and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B REPOS_DIR\fR / \fBUSE_REPOS_BIND
Gentoo repository path and optional bind mount.
.TP
.B USE_GENTOO_PATCHES_BIND
Bind
.I /etc/portage/patches
from the host when
.B YES
and the host path exists.
.TP
.B EXTRA_BIND_MOUNT
Semicolon-separated list of absolute host paths to bind into the chroot.
Protected system roots are rejected.
.SH SHARED FILE CACHE
When
.B USE_CCACHE_FILE=YES
and/or
.B USE_SCCACHE_FILE=YES ,
each cache type uses a
.B shared tmpfs
workspace so multiple concurrent
.B use
/
.B rebase
instances can share one hot cache.
.PP
Default workspace roots (overridable via environment):
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-ccache
Shared ccache workspace
.RB ( CCACHE_SHARE_ROOT ).
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-sccache
Shared sccache workspace
.RB ( SCCACHE_SHARE_ROOT ).
.TP
.B /tmp/StormByte-cache-locks
Lock and holder metadata
.RB ( CACHE_LOCK_DIR ).
.PP
Lifecycle per cache type:
.IP \(bu 3
The
.B first
concurrent session creates the tmpfs (size
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE
/
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE ,
defaulting to
.B STORAGE_SIZE
or
.BR 8G ),
unpacks the sidecar
.I .tbz2
if it exists, and records itself as a holder.
.IP \(bu 3
Later sessions bind the same workspace into their stage tree and join the
holder list.
.B flock
plus a holders file of live PIDs; dead PIDs are pruned.
.IP \(bu 3
On exit, each session drops itself. The
.B last
session packs the workspace back into the sidecar and unmounts the tmpfs.
.IP \(bu 3
Packing is
.B independent
of
.RB \(lq Save changes? \(rq .
.IP \(bu 3
sccache's server is stopped before any unmount.
.IP \(bu 3
Emergency cleanup on
.BR EXIT / INT / TERM / HUP
stops sccache, drops stage-side binds, and runs the last-holder pack when this
PID was a holder.
.PP
Missing sidecars on first use are not an error.
.SH GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B DRY_RUN=1
Simulate heavy or destructive actions without applying them.
.TP
.B FORCE=1
Skip interactive confirmations. Mapped to
.B CONFIRM=1
for
.B confirm_yes
from
.IR functions.sh .
.TP
.B SKIP_CACHE=1
Skip shared FILE cache acquire and last-holder pack for this run.
.TP
.B TARBALL_FOLDER=\fI/path\fR
Override
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
for this run (also
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER_OVERRIDE ).
.TP
.B STORAGE_SYSTEM=\fIvalue\fR
Override storage backend for
.B use
/
.B rebase
(ignored by
.B convert
/
.BR export ).
.TP
.B STORAGE_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Override size for
.B zram
/
.B tmpfs
and the default shared cache tmpfs size.
.TP
.B CCACHE_SHARE_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override shared ccache tmpfs mountpoint (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-ccache ).
.TP
.B SCCACHE_SHARE_ROOT=\fI/path\fR
Override shared sccache tmpfs mountpoint (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-sccache ).
.TP
.B CACHE_LOCK_DIR=\fI/path\fR
Override directory for cache lock/holder files (default
.IR /tmp/StormByte-cache-locks ).
.TP
.B CCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Size of the shared ccache tmpfs (e.g.
.BR 8G ).
.TP
.B SCCACHE_TMPFS_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
Size of the shared sccache tmpfs.
.TP
.B SCCACHE_CACHE_SIZE=\fIvalue\fR
sccache budget exported into the chroot (default
.BR 20G ).
.SH STAGE SELECTION
Commands that take a stage accept either:
.TP
.B <index>
Zero-based index as shown by
.BR list .
.TP
.B <filename>
Basename or path relative to
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER ,
or an absolute path to an existing stage file.
.PP
Recognised extensions (read):
.BR tar.gz ,
.BR tgz ,
.BR tgzip ,
.BR tar.bz2 ,
.BR tbz2 ,
.BR tbzip2 ,
.BR tar.xz ,
.BR txz ,
.BR tar.zstd ,
.BR tar.zst ,
.BR tzstd ,
.BR tzd .
.PP
Canonical extensions written by
.B convert
:
.BR tgzip ,
.BR tbzip2 ,
.BR txz ,
.BR tzd .
.B export
always writes
.BR txz .
.PP
Sidecar files
.I ccache.tbz2
and
.I sccache.tbz2
are never listed as stages.
.SH COMPRESSION FORMATS
.TP
.B gzip
Write
.BR tgzip .
Also reads
.BR tar.gz / tgz .
.TP
.B bzip2
Write
.BR tbzip2 .
Also reads
.BR tar.bz2 / tbz2 .
.TP
.B xz
Write
.BR txz .
Also reads
.BR tar.xz .
.TP
.B zstd
Write
.BR tzd .
Also reads
.BR tzstd / tar.zst / tar.zstd .
.PP
.B convert
and
.B export
take format
.IR names
.RB ( gzip | bzip2 | xz | zstd ),
not extensions.
Same source and destination codec is a
.B copy
.RB ( cp \-\-reflink=auto ,
fallback
.BR cp ),
not a recompress.
Different codecs stream
.B pv | decompress | compress
onto a
.I .partial
file and
.B mv
into place. Ctrl-C deletes the partial only.
.PP
Parallel tools are used when present
.RB ( pigz ,
.BR lbzip2 ,
.BR pxz ,
.BR pzstd ).
.B pv
is required.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS list (alias: ls)
.TP
.B list
List stages in
.B TARBALL_FOLDER
(recursive) with index, size, mtime, and flags for notes and lock files.
Does not require root.
.SS use
.TP
.B use \fI<index|filename>
Requires root (re-exec via
.B sudo \-E
if needed).
Lock the stage, extract into temporary storage, apply bind mounts and optional
caches, enter an interactive chroot, then unmount, clean Portage temporary
data, optionally save the stage tarball, release shared FILE caches, and unlock.
.PP
On exit from the chroot the user is prompted to save
.B stage
changes.
Compiler caches in FILE mode are packed by the last concurrent session
regardless of that answer.
.SS rebase
.TP
.B rebase \fI<index|filename> <new_file_name>
Same workflow as
.BR use .
The save target is
.I new_file_name
under
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER
(need not exist yet). Compression is taken from that name's extension.
.SS convert
.TP
.B convert \fI<index|filename> <compression_format>
Stream-recompress (or copy if the codec is unchanged) next to the original.
Writes the canonical short extension.
Fails if the target path already exists, except when source and destination
are the same file (no-op).
Does not extract, does not mount
.BR STORAGE_* ,
does not require root.
.SS export
.TP
.B export \fI<index|filename> <destination_folder>
Same stream path as
.BR convert .
Always
.BR xz .
Output name is
.BI <stem> - YYYYMMDD .txz
in an existing
.IR destination_folder .
No format argument.
Does not require root.
.SS delete (alias: rm)
.TP
.B delete \fI<index|filename>
Delete the stage file (and notes sidecar if present) after confirmation.
.SS rename
.TP
.B rename \fI<index|filename> <new_file_name>
Rename the stage within
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
Notes sidecar is renamed when present.
.SS download
.TP
.B download \fI<arch>\fR [\fIprofile\fR]
Download an official Gentoo stage3 (default profile:
.BR default ).
Retries transient failures; verifies
.B DIGESTS
when available (SHA-512 preferred, else SHA-256).
Writes into a temporary file and
.B mv
into
.BR TARBALL_FOLDER .
Does not require root if that folder is writable.
.PP
Architectures and profiles match
.BR "help download" .
.SS notes
.TP
.B notes list
List stages that have a
.I .notes
sidecar.
.TP
.B notes \fI<index|filename> edit
Open notes with
.BR TARBALL_NOTE_EDITOR .
.TP
.B notes \fI<index|filename> delete
Remove the notes file for that stage.
.SS config
.TP
.B config
Print resolved configuration.
.SS help
.TP
.B help
Built-in usage summary.
.TP
.B help \fI<command>
Detailed help for one command.
.TP
.B help compression
Formats and extensions.
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR, \fB\-V
Print program name and version, then exit.
.SH LOCKING AND CLEANUP
Per-stage lock files live under
.I /tmp
as
.BI . <tarball-basename> .lock
and prevent concurrent
.B use
/
.B rebase
of the
.B same
basename.
Shared FILE caches allow concurrent sessions across stages.
.PP
On
.BR EXIT ,
.BR INT ,
.B TERM
and
.BR HUP
an idempotent cleanup runs
.B only
for resources this PID created:
stop sccache, unmount stage binds (pkg/distfiles/repos/patches/extra, cache
binds, /proc /dev /sys /run), last-holder FILE pack, unmount the tmp tree,
reset zram only if this PID allocated it
.B and
the mount is gone, delete
.I .partial
/
.I .compress
scratch files, remove the stage lock.
A directory that is still a mountpoint is
.B not
.BR rm \-rf 'd.
.B list
/
.B help
/
.B config
leave every inventory flag at 0, so the trap is a no-op.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (including a declined confirmation that takes no action).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error.
.TP
.B 2
Runtime failure (configuration, I/O, mount, download, or integrity check).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/conf.d/StormByte-StageManager.conf
System configuration.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/*.{tgzip,tbzip2,txz,tzd,\fR...}
Stage archives.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/*.notes
Per-stage notes.
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/ccache.tbz2
Packed ccache sidecar (FILE mode).
.TP
.I TARBALL_FOLDER/sccache.tbz2
Packed sccache sidecar (FILE mode).
.TP
.I /tmp/.<basename>.lock
Per-stage lock.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chroot (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR zstd (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR zramctl (8)
